# A fast subset of `make ci`, not a copy of it. Anything slower than a few
# seconds gets bypassed with --no-verify, which is worse than not having it.
# Warm this is about four seconds; cold it is however long one turbo build takes.
#
# `make` before a PR remains the real gate. This only catches the mistakes that
# are cheap to catch.
./scripts/assert-ts-version.sh
./scripts/check-env-example.sh
./scripts/check-app-boundaries.sh
pnpm exec turbo run lint typecheck
